Charter: #719

## Task: Live acceptance — click-to-detail (scenario b)

API-level proof that click-to-detail data from #691 is present on the deployed cockpit.

**Context:** Charter #719 requires live acceptance of #691's two scenarios. This leaf covers scenario (b): clicking an element (queue/board/agent) opens a detail panel showing full title, issue body (`d.body`), status/stage, last verdict/comment, and GitHub link. Acceptance is via API responses (no browser required) since the deployment box has no Chromium installed. Browser pass is optional if Chromium is available. A cold executor sees only this issue — all required context is below.

**Known API facts (from crewboss-api.py do_GET, lines 860-899):**
- `/api/state` — returns full board state; task numbers are in field `.n` (NOT `.id`)
- `/api/task/N` — returns task detail including `body` field (singular, by number)
- `/api/comments/N` — returns `{"ok": true, "comments": [...]}` — an **object**, not an array
- There is NO `/api/tasks` (plural) list endpoint — it returns 404

## Steps

**Step 1 — Code read:**
Read `ui/app/src/App.tsx` around line 1283. Confirm `d.body` rendering is wired (code read is sufficient proof for rendering wire-up).

**Step 2 — Get a live task number N from /api/state:**
```
N=$(curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $CB_API_TOKEN" http://localhost:8787/api/state \
  | jq -r '[.board[] | select(.kind=="leaf")] | .[0].n')
echo "Using task N=$N"
```
Use N in subsequent calls. The field is `.n` (not `.id`).

**Step 3 — API proof for task body:**
```
curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $CB_API_TOKEN" http://localhost:8787/api/task/$N \
  | jq -e '.body | length > 0'
```
Assert the `body` field is non-empty (jq exits 0 if true).

**Step 4 — API proof for comments/last verdict:**
```
curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $CB_API_TOKEN" http://localhost:8787/api/comments/$N \
  | jq -e '.comments | length > 0'
```
Assert at least one comment is present. **Important:** The response is `{"ok":true,"comments":[...]}` — an object, not an array. Use `.comments | length > 0` (NOT bare `length > 0`, which counts object keys and is always 2, making the check a false-positive).

**Step 5 — Log responses as proof.** If any field is missing or empty, note it and open a follow-up leaf.

**Step 6 — Browser pass (optional):** Only if `which chromium` returns a path, do a full browser pass: click one element from each panel type (queue item, board item, agent), verify the detail panel opens with full title, issue body, status/stage, last verdict/comment, and a GitHub link.

